            <td>Independent controller: Sign in with Google</td>
            <td>Google account identifier and email address</td>
            <td>Ireland and the USA, under Google's privacy policy</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>GitHub, Inc.</td>
            <td>Hosting the app's downloads and updates</td>
            <td>IP address and browser or app information when you download the app or it checks for updates</td>
            <td>USA; EU–US Data Privacy Framework, under GitHub's privacy statement</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Hugging Face, Inc.</td>
            <td>Hosting the on-device speech models the Mac app downloads when it first needs them (such as the WhisperKit model, about 630 MB)</td>
            <td>IP address and app information when the app downloads a model</td>
            <td>USA, under Hugging Face's privacy policy</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Zoner Oy</td>
            <td>Processor: hosting our email</td>
            <td>Emails you send us and our replies</td>
            <td>Finland (EU)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      <strong>AI assistants you connect.</strong> If you turn on AI assistant access and connect an assistant such as
      Claude (Anthropic) or ChatGPT (OpenAI), its provider is not our sub-processor: you choose and connect it, and the
      provider handles what the assistant reads from your notes under its own terms and privacy policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>International transfers.</strong> When personal data is transferred outside the EU and EEA, we rely on the
      European Commission's adequacy decision for the EU–US Data Privacy Framework where the recipient is certified under
      it, and otherwise on the Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses included in the provider's data processing terms.
      You can ask us for a copy of the relevant safeguards.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Payments.</strong> Subscriptions are sold through Link, Stripe's payment service, which is the merchant of
      record for your purchase; your card statement shows <code>{cardStatementDescriptor}</code>. Stripe and Link process
      your payment, billing and tax details as independent controllers under the{" "}
      <a href={stripePrivacyUrl}>Stripe privacy policy</a> and <a href={linkPrivacyUrl}>Link's privacy policy</a>, and the
      purchase itself is governed by <a href={linkTermsUrl}>Link's terms</a>. From them we receive only your Stripe customer
      ID, your subscription status and period, the amounts of your invoices and refunds (with currency, discount and tax)
      and, if you cancel and give one, your cancellation reason — never your card details. Subscriptions bought in the
      iPhone app are sold and billed by Apple through the App Store under its own terms and the{" "}
      <a href={applePrivacyUrl}>Apple privacy policy</a>; RevenueCat checks those purchases for us as our processor. From
      them we receive only the product, status and period of your App Store subscription — never your Apple Account or
      payment details. We do not sell personal data or share it for advertising.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection sections={sections} id="retention">
    <ul>
      <li>
        Meeting content: no audio, notes or translations are stored on our servers, except the AI assistant copy if you
        turn that on (below); the final transcript is kept
        encrypted so it can be re-sent for 2 hours (see section 3), then deleted at the next daily cleanup (within about a
        day). At our AI providers: Deepgram keeps the live audio and
        transcript only
        while processing them; Anthropic deletes it within 30 days (up to 2 years if flagged under its usage policy);
        ElevenLabs keeps it under its own retention rules (see section 8).
      </li>
      <li>
        The encrypted sync copy (only if you turn on sync): while sync is on. Turning sync off deletes it immediately. A
        meeting or chat you delete is removed from storage right away; a small marker that it was deleted (identifier,
        type and time, no content) is kept for 90 days so your other devices delete their copy too. If your subscription
        ends, your devices can still download or delete the copy for 90 days; after that it is deleted automatically.
      </li>
      <li>
        Shared notes (only if you share a note with a link): until the link expires (7, 30 or 90 days, as you choose),
        you remove it or you delete the meeting in the app, whichever comes first. A removed link is deleted at once; an
        expired one stops working at once and is deleted at the next daily cleanup (within about a day).
      </li>
      <li>
        The AI assistant copy (only if you turn on AI assistant access): while the setting is on. Turning it off deletes it
        immediately and disconnects every assistant; a meeting you delete, or a device's meetings you remove, is removed
        from it right away. If your subscription or trial ends, assistants lose access immediately and the copy is deleted
        within 7 days. Deleting your account deletes it with the account. Backups: gone within 30 days. Connection records:
        until you disconnect the assistant, turn the setting off or delete your account; in Workers KV also no longer than
        the connection lasts (30 days without use, at most 180 days).
      </li>
      <li>
        Account and sign-in identities: while your account exists; deleted immediately when you delete it. Device
        registrations: the same, and also deleted after 13 months without use.
      </li>
      <li>Meeting session records and monthly usage: up to 13 months, then deleted automatically; deleted immediately when you delete your account.</li>
      <li>
        A meeting's live-transcript figures (when the first access key was issued, how many were issued and the streaming
        seconds counted): when the meeting session record is deleted (after 13 months, or when you delete your account),
        their link to the meeting is replaced with a random identifier, so they are no longer linked to you or your
        meetings; they are then kept without a time limit, because the live-transcript capacity we set aside is a fixed
        total that they count against.
      </li>
      <li>
        The pseudonymous free-trial record (a keyed hash of your sign-in identity, the number of free-trial meetings used,
        when the trial started and that month's usage totals): for up to 24 months after you delete your account, then
        deleted automatically; the usage totals only matter until the end of that month.
      </li>
      <li>The DeviceCheck bit for your Mac or iPhone is stored by Apple, not by us; it holds no personal details, only that the device has already given a free trial.</li>
      <li>Sign-in tokens: up to 60 days; deleted within a day after they expire or you sign out.</li>
      <li>
        The Sign in with Apple refresh token: while your account exists (replaced each time you sign in with Apple);
        revoked with Apple and deleted when you delete your account. If a sign-in is abandoned before an account is
        created, it is deleted within a day.
      </li>
      <li>Your account's daily usage counters (used for the daily limits): 2 days. The hashed IP records for new trials and for counting downloads: until the end of that day.</li>
      <li>Contact messages, feedback and crash reports: 180 days. Emails: for as long as needed to handle your request.</li>
      <li>Cancellation reasons and comments: 180 days; deleted immediately when you delete your account.</li>
      <li>
        Invite records: while the accounts involved exist. When you delete your account, your invite code and the records
        that link an invite to your account are deleted; for an account that used an invite, the keyed hashes of its
        sign-in identity and of the card fingerprint, and the dates, are kept for up to 24 months so the same person or
        card can't use an invite again.
      </li>
      <li>Processed payment events and total daily AI spend (not linked to you): 90 days.</li>
      <li>Daily download source, campaign, error, AI token and transcription language totals and daily usage statistics (not linked to you): 400 days.</li>
      <li>
        The total number of app downloads per day and the number of refused free-trial starts per day and reason: these
        aggregate totals hold only the date, a count and, for refusals, the reason; they contain no personal data and are
        kept without a time limit for business statistics.
      </li>
      <li>
        Daily overall totals for running the business, such as the number of accounts, active accounts, meetings, trials
        and subscriptions and the monthly revenue (not linked to anyone): 5 years.
      </li>
      <li>The latest app and OS version on your account, the time the app last checked in and the date of the last daily usage report: while your account exists; deleted immediately when you delete it.</li>
      <li>Technical logs: kept for a short period by Cloudflare, normally no more than a few days.</li>
      <li>Database backups (Cloudflare D1 point-in-time recovery): up to 30 days, after which deleted data is gone from backups too.</li>
      <li>
        Our accounting records of subscription income, including the invoice and refund amounts we receive from Stripe:
        for as long as Finnish accounting law requires (currently up to 10 years); when you delete your account they are
        no longer linked to it. Receipts and payment records are kept by Stripe and Link under their own policies.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection sections={sections} id="deletion">
    <p>
      You can delete your account at any time with “Delete account” on your <a href={routes.account}>account page</a>,
      or in the Mac or iPhone app under Settings › Account.
      Any unfinished subscription is first cancelled immediately at Stripe; then your account, sign-in identities,
      sessions, device registrations, meeting session records, usage, subscription records (including the App Store
      subscription record), cancellation reasons, invite code and invite records linked to your account, Stripe
      customer link, the records of the encrypted sync copy and every note you shared with a link are deleted together
      in a single step (shared links stop working at once); the encrypted copy
      itself is removed from storage at once (or, if storage can't be reached, at the next daily cleanup). If you turned on
      AI assistant access, its copy of your notes is deleted in the same way and every connected assistant loses access. If you signed in with Apple, we first ask Apple to revoke
      Gistsmith's access to your Apple ID, using the token we stored for that; the account is deleted even if Apple can't
      be reached, and we then follow up manually. You can also stop using Sign in with Apple for Gistsmith yourself, in
      your Apple ID settings (on iPhone: Settings › your name › Sign-In &amp; Security › Sign in with Apple).
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>App Store subscriptions are not cancelled by deleting your account.</strong> Only you can cancel them, with
      Apple: on your iPhone in Settings › your name › Subscriptions. Until you do, Apple keeps billing you, and Apple and
      RevenueCat keep the purchase records under their own policies (RevenueCat's linked to your former account ID; ask
      us and we will have RevenueCat delete them).
    </p>
    <p>
      What remains: a pseudonymous record of your free-trial use (a keyed one-way hash of your sign-in identity, the
      number of free-trial meetings used, when the trial started, whether a device was verified and that month's usage
      totals), kept for up to 24 months to prevent abuse — if you sign in again with the same Apple or Google account, your
      new account continues the trial where the old one left off and, within the same month, starts from the old
      account's usage; the DeviceCheck bit for your device, which Apple stores; today's trial and download counters for
      your network (a hashed IP address, not linked to any account, deleted at the end of the day); the live-transcript
      figures of your meetings (when access keys were issued and the streaming seconds counted), with their meeting link
      replaced by a random identifier so they are no longer linked to you; if your account used an
      invite code, keyed hashes of your sign-in identity and of the paying card's fingerprint with the dates, for up to
      24 months; payment records kept by
      Stripe and Link, and our accounting records of your invoice and refund amounts, no longer linked to your account; messages you sent through the contact form until their 180 days run out (ask us if you want them
      deleted sooner — feedback and crash reports linked to your account are deleted with it); if a duplicate
      subscription was ever created by mistake, its Stripe identifiers for up to 400 days so a double charge can be
      refunded; and
      technical logs and backups until they expire. Notes and recordings on your Mac or iPhone stay where they are; you delete them
      in the app.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection sections={sections} id="rights">
    <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>access the personal data we hold about you and get a copy of it;</li>
      <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
      <li>have your data erased;</li>
      <li>restrict processing;</li>
      <li>receive the data you gave us in a portable format;</li>
      <li>object to processing based on legitimate interest.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Write to <a href={mail}>{operator.email}</a>. We may ask you to confirm that the account is yours, and we reply
      within one month. If you took part in a meeting that someone else recorded, contact that person first (see section
      3). You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority — in Finland, the Office of the Data
      Protection Ombudsman (Tietosuojavaltuutetun toimisto, <a href="https://tietosuoja.fi/en">tietosuoja.fi</a>), or the
      authority in the EU country where you live or work.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection sections={sections} id="security">
    <p>
      All connections are encrypted with TLS. Sign-in tokens are stored on our server only as one-way hashes and IP
      addresses only as keyed hashes. Free trials are checked with Apple DeviceCheck, and requests from the app with Apple
      App Attest where the Mac supports it (the iPhone app does not use App Attest). Our provider keys exist only
      as encrypted secrets on our server, and access to the service's systems is limited to the operator.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection sections={sections} id="decisions">
    <p>
      We don't make decisions about you based solely on automated processing that have legal or similarly significant
      effects. Usage limits are applied automatically according to your plan, as described in the{" "}
      <a href={routes.terms}>Terms of service</a>.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection sections={sections} id="children">
    <p>{productName} is not intended for anyone under 18, and we don't knowingly process children's data.</p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection sections={sections} id="changes">
    <p>
      When we change this policy we update the date at the top. We announce material changes in the app and on this
      page before they take effect.
    </p>
  </LegalSection>

  <LegalSection sections={sections} id="contact">
    <p>
      {operator.name}<br />
      {operator.address}<br />
      Business ID {operator.businessId}<br />
      <a href={mail}>{operator.email}</a>
    </p>
  </LegalSection>
</Legal>

